' Screen contract.
'
' Every screen in the app is a SceneGraph component (extends Group) that owns
' its whole visible surface and its own onKeyEvent. Roku screens cannot extend
' a BrightScript class, so the contract is enforced by convention and invoked
' by the ScreenStack through callFunc on the node:
'
'   function OnEnter(params as object)  - called when the screen is pushed or
'                                         restored; params is invalid when it is
'                                         only being uncovered by a pop.
'   function OnExit()                   - called when the screen is popped.
'   function OnBackPressed() as boolean - true means the screen swallowed Back
'                                         (e.g. a backdrop or dialog inside it);
'                                         false lets the stack pop the screen.
'   function BlurFocus()                - drop any inline focus the screen holds
'                                         (chips, secondary lists) so a blurred
'                                         node never eats OK/arrow keys again.
'
' Rules screens follow:
'   - screen-level keys are their own; cross-screen navigation happens ONLY by
'     publishing an action / calling the stack, never by driving a sibling.
'   - inline controls (chip rows, season tabs) exit via Back or Down; they are
'     not navigation modes.
'   - the scene dispatches actions; it never re-dispatches list itemSelected.

' Debug identity helper: report a screen node without touching node fields.
function ScreenDebugName(node as object) as string
    if node = invalid then return "<invalid>"
    return node.id
end function